course: dictionary
lesson: 6923
title: Packaging: the wrapping and the look
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Packaging is the boxes, bags, plastic and paper that things are wrapped in when you buy them. Read the words around it to check. «Packaging can make things look bigger than they are; the weight on the label tells the truth.» The box is the packaging, and the sentence warns you that a big box can fool you about how much is inside.
explain: The word has a second meaning: the way something is presented to make it look attractive. «"Limited edition" often means the same product in new packaging, sold to make you buy it now.» The product is the same, but its look has changed to tempt you. Ask yourself: is the sentence talking about the wrapping itself, or about how it is dressed up to sell?
explain: Packaging is often too much, and it creates waste. In science lessons you sort it for recycling, such as cardboard, plastic, glass and metal. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense: «too much wrapping» works just as well as «too much packaging».
fact: Packaging means the boxes, bags, plastic and paper that things are wrapped in.
fact: «Packaging» can also mean the way something is presented to look attractive.
fact: Common phrases include «plastic packaging», «too much packaging» and «recyclable packaging».
fact: Packaging creates waste, so people sort it for recycling: cardboard, plastic, glass and metal.
fact: Plastic packaging must be kept away from babies, because it can cause suffocation.
exercise: «Packaging can make things look bigger than they are.» In this sentence, what is packaging? | A type of tree that grows tall | The shop where you pay | The sound a thing makes | *The box or wrapping around a thing
exercise: Which of these can be sorted from packaging for recycling? | Sand | Sunshine | *Glass | Feathers
exercise: «"Limited edition" often means the same product in new packaging, sold to make you buy it now.» What is the main reason the packaging is changed? | To stop people recycling it | To shorten the product's name | To make the product weigh less | *To make you want to buy it now
test: «Too much packaging» is a problem because it creates what? | *Waste | Sunshine | Music | Gold
test: Why must plastic packaging be kept away from babies? | It makes them grow faster | It is too heavy to lift | It tastes sweet | *It can cause suffocation
exam: Packaging can make things look bigger than they are; what tells you the truth about how much is inside? | The name of the shop | *The weight on the label | The shape of the wrapping | The colour of the box
